ans_lst=[None]*N
for n in range(N):
    ans_lst[n]=S0-S1+ST.Fold(0,idx[n])+ST1.Fold(idx[n]+1,K)
    ans_lst[n]%=mod
    if idx[n]<K:
        ST[idx[n]]=0
        ans_lst[n]+=1
for n in range(N):
    ans_lst[n]%=mod
print(*ans_lst,sep="\n")
```

The key fix: in `Build_Fact`, when `self.e==None`, the inverse loop should simply multiply by `(i+1)` without the `while ii%self.p==0` check (which was comparing against the modulus and is unnecessary). This removes per-iteration overhead. I also hoisted the constant `Fact_Inve` calls out of the loops and avoided computing `ST.Fold` twice.
